              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>It can act as an <strong>agonist</strong>, acting like the natural ligand, and performing the same physiological response as the natural ligand.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>It can act as an <strong>antagonist</strong>, binding to the receptor and just blocking it, competing with the natural ligand and thereby decreasing the messages that are sent to the cell.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>On <em>certain receptors,</em> it can act as an <strong>inverse agonist</strong>, which is simplistically referred to by many authors as an antagonist.&nbsp;</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>No, the term 'inhibitor' is the term that we use for drugs that <strong>inhibit enzymes</strong>. In this chapter, we are discussing <strong>cellular receptors</strong>. Module 1 Chapter 4 discusses enzymatic inhibitors.&nbsp;</div>\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "<div>Indeed,&nbsp;the term 'inhibitor' is the term that we use for drugs that <strong>inhibit enzymes</strong>. In this chapter, we are discussing <strong>cellular receptors</strong>. Module 1 Chapter 4 discusses enzymatic inhibitors.</div>\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>It can act as an inhibitor</div>\n"
                }
